{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they said</b> — the commentator says: they sought to know what people he was and what land, lest a decree of death had been decreed upon them from heaven — this is not correct. For if HaShem decreed upon a people, if there was not even one of them upon whom it was decreed, but only in another place among other people, why would the others fear, as though they would intermingle with one upon whom He decreed alone to die? And the way of most people is to live by their labor, and a person's trade testifies about him, and why would he enter to go to a specific place — and there are lands whose people are mostly good, and so it is known today."], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:59.279525113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}